SpaceCatalog data releases — licence
====================================

This repository distributes data compiled from published astronomical
catalogues. It is not under a single licence, and no statement here
can replace the terms of the upstream a given row came from.

Every row in objects.csv names its upstream in the `source` column, and
sources.csv in the same release gives that upstream's terms. Those
terms govern the row. The set for this release:

  CC BY 4.0 (VizieR)
      gcvs, wds
  CC BY 4.0 (VizieR); see each catalogue's own reference
      deepsky_distances
  CC BY-SA 3.0 IGO
      gaia_dr3, gaia_dr3_sky
  CC-BY-4.0
      curated
  CC-BY-SA-4.0
      hyg, openngc
  CC0 1.0
      wikidata
  IAU Minor Planet Center; free to use with attribution
      mpc
  ODbL
      simbad
  Public domain (NASA)
      exoplanet_archive
  Public domain (NASA/JPL)
      jpl_sats, jpl_sbdb
  VizieR terms; cite Dalya+ 2022 (2022MNRAS.514.1403D)
      glade_plus, glade_plus_sky

Share-alike terms in that set reach anything derived from the rows
they cover. If you redistribute a subset, check which upstreams it
drew from rather than which licence this file mentions first.

Attribution
-----------

Cite the release. Citing the release does not discharge the upstream
attribution: see https://spacecatalog.org/releases for both, with a worked example.

The pipeline that produced these files is separate from the data and
is licensed Apache-2.0.
